---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { extractFaqItems } from '../utils/schema-helpers';
import { withSiteUtm } from '../lib/site-utm.mjs';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const tipsPlusHref = withSiteUtm('https://account.powerbi.tips', 'power-designer');
const themeCiteHref = `${base}/power-bi-theme-generator/`;

const title = 'Power Designer: Power BI report design in Fabric';
const description = 'What is Power Designer?';

// Owned H2 + five FAQ H3s. extractFaqItems reads this string; do not add
// Entity as ## / ### (that heading would become a junk FAQPage item).
const citeFaqMarkdown = `## What is Power Designer?

**TL;DR.** Power Designer is the Tips+ report-design tool for Power BI and Fabric. Build wireframes, layouts, and themes, including AI auto-layout, then export a PBIP for Desktop. It is not the free Theme Generator, and it is not Entelexos.

### What does Power Designer include?

Wireframes, page layouts, theme and palette controls, gallery templates, and AI visual auto-layout. You leave with a designed report file for a model author, not a finished semantic model.

### How is Power Designer different from the Theme Generator?

The Theme Generator is the free visual editor that writes Power BI theme JSON. Power Designer is the Tips+ design product (web and Fabric workload) for pages, layouts, and gallery projects. Use the generator for a theme file; use Power Designer when you need the page.

### What does Tips+ have to do with it?

Power Designer unlocks with a Tips+ license. Manage that at the PowerBI.tips account portal. Tips+ is separate from a Microsoft Pro, PPU, or Fabric capacity license.

### Does Power Designer run in Microsoft Fabric?

Yes. Power Designer is also offered as a Fabric workload (Tips+ License & Power Designer on AppSource). Your tenant still has to allow the workload. The web / Tips+ app is the other entry.

### How do I get a Power Designer file into Power BI Desktop?

Export the project as a PBIP, extract it, and open it in Desktop. Tutorials on this site walk through gallery copy/edit and AI visual objects.
`;

const faqItems = extractFaqItems(citeFaqMarkdown);
const faqJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqItems.map((item) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: item.question,
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: item.answer,
    },
  })),
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={faqJsonLd}>
  <article>
    <section class="mb-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900">{title}</h1>
    </section>

    <section class="prose max-w-none">
      <h2>What is Power Designer?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>TL;DR.</strong> Power Designer is the Tips+ report-design tool for Power BI and Fabric.
        Build wireframes, layouts, and themes, including AI auto-layout, then export a PBIP for
        Desktop. It is not the free Theme Generator, and it is not Entelexos.
      </p>
    </section>

    <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-4">
        <dt class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">What</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-neutral-700">
          Tips+ report-design tool for Power BI / Fabric: wireframes, layouts, themes, gallery, AI
          auto-layout; export PBIP.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-4">
        <dt class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Who</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-neutral-700">
          Report authors who do not want to build every page by hand.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-4">
        <dt class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Cost</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-neutral-700">
          Tips+ (account.powerbi.tips). No invented price. Separate from Pro / PPU / Fabric capacity.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-4">
        <dt class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Not</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-neutral-700">
          Not Microsoft. Not the free Theme Generator. Not Entelexos.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <section class="prose max-w-none mt-10">
      <h3>What does Power Designer include?</h3>
      <p>
        Wireframes, page layouts, theme and palette controls, gallery templates, and AI visual
        auto-layout. You leave with a designed report file for a model author, not a finished
        semantic model.
      </p>

      <h3>How is Power Designer different from the Theme Generator?</h3>
      <p>
        The Theme Generator is the free visual editor that writes Power BI theme JSON. Power Designer
        is the Tips+ design product (web and Fabric workload) for pages, layouts, and gallery
        projects. Use the generator for a theme file; use Power Designer when you need the page.
      </p>

      <h3>What does Tips+ have to do with it?</h3>
      <p>
        Power Designer unlocks with a Tips+ license. Manage that at the PowerBI.tips account portal.
        Tips+ is separate from a Microsoft Pro, PPU, or Fabric capacity license.
      </p>

      <h3>Does Power Designer run in Microsoft Fabric?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. Power Designer is also offered as a Fabric workload (Tips+ License & Power Designer on
        AppSource). Your tenant still has to allow the workload. The web / Tips+ app is the other
        entry.
      </p>

      <h3>How do I get a Power Designer file into Power BI Desktop?</h3>
      <p>
        Export the project as a PBIP, extract it, and open it in Desktop. Tutorials on this site walk
        through gallery copy/edit and AI visual objects.
      </p>
    </section>

    <ul class="mt-8 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6 text-neutral-700">
      <li>Wireframes</li>
      <li>Layouts</li>
      <li>Themes</li>
      <li>Gallery</li>
      <li>AI auto-layout</li>
      <li>PBIP export</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-neutral-700">
      Entelexos is a different product (white-label embed), not this page.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a
        class="rounded-full bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-blue-700"
        href={tipsPlusHref}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Start with Tips+
      </a>
      <a
        class="rounded-full bg-neutral-100 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-neutral-900 hover:bg-neutral-200"
        href={themeCiteHref}
      >
        What is the Power BI Theme Generator?
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-neutral-700">
      Related:
      <a class="font-medium text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800" href={`${base}/2024/04/29/tips-theme-generator-tutorial-automatic-visual-objects-with-ai/`}>Tips+ Designer Tutorial: Automatic Visual Objects with AI</a>,
      <a class="font-medium text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800" href={`${base}/2024/02/27/tips-theme-generator-tutorial-gallery-project-copy-edit/`}>Tips+ Designer Tutorial: Gallery Project Copy &amp; Edit</a>,
      <a class="font-medium text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800" href={themeCiteHref}>What is the Power BI Theme Generator?</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
